<h2 id="when-to-see-a-doctor">When to see a doctor</h2>

<p>An early return to exercise, a knock or a drink often causes nothing more than a sore or swollen day. Contact the clinic the same day, rather than waiting for a review, if you notice any of these:</p>

<ul>
  <li>bleeding that does not stop with ten minutes of gentle, steady pressure;</li>
  <li>a graft that has visibly come out, especially with fresh bleeding from the site;</li>
  <li>swelling that spreads, or is still worsening after about day four;</li>
  <li>pain that increases after the first few days instead of settling;</li>
  <li>fever, spreading redness and warmth, pus or a bad smell from either area.</li>
</ul>

<p>A hard knock to the head followed by headache, vomiting, drowsiness or confusion needs urgent medical attention, whatever the state of the grafts. Shedding of the transplanted hairs from about week two is different: it is expected, and <a href="/blog/shedding-and-shock-loss-after-hair-transplant">why transplanted hair falls out</a> explains it. <a href="/blog/hair-transplant-side-effects-and-risks">Hair transplant side effects and risks</a> separates what is expected from what is not.</p>

<h2 id="getting-it-assessed">Getting it assessed</h2>

<p>The right timings for you depend on the technique used, the size of the session, how your scalp heals and what your days involve, which is why they are confirmed at your reviews rather than read off a table. Consultations with registered medical practitioners are available at our clinics in Sector 39, Gurugram and Rohini, Delhi. <a href="/hair-transplant-in-gurgaon">Hair transplant in Gurgaon</a> and <a href="/hair-transplant-delhi/rohini">hair transplant in Rohini</a> set out how a procedure and its follow-up are planned, and bringing your work pattern, commute and sport to the consultation lets the recovery be planned around them from the start.</p>

